fit and well. She denies any fever, chills, or significant weight loss. She has been a regular smoker and drinks socially on weekends. She denies any drug use.\n\n**Review of Systems (ROS):**\n- **General:** No fever, chills, or weight loss.\n- **Gastrointestinal:** Occasional crampy lower abdominal pain, denies nausea or vomiting.\n- **Genitourinary:** Moderate burning sensation while urinating, slight darkening of urine.\n- **Other systems:** Denies back pain, denies any other significant symptoms.\n\n**2. Objective:**\n- **General:** Alert and oriented, no acute distress.\n- **Abdominal Exam:** Mild tenderness in the suprapubic area, no rebound tenderness or guarding.\n- **Vital Signs:** Not taken during this visit.\n- **Investigations:** Urine dipstick test positive for leukocytes and nitrites.\n- **Awaiting:** Urine culture and sensitivity test results.\n\n**3. Assessment:**\n- Unspecified symptoms and signs involving the genitourinary system (R39.9).\n- Likely UTI, given the burning sensation, crampy lower abdominal pain, and positive urine dipstick for leukocytes and nitrites.\n\n**4. Plan:**\n- **Medication:** Prescribed Nitrofurantoin 100 mg, 1 tablet, twice a day, for 3 days, oral route.\n- **Follow-up:** Advised to return if symptoms persist or worsen.\n- **Lifestyle Recommendations:** Advised to drink plenty of fluids, try cranberry juice, and avoid irritants.\n- **Referral:** None at this time.\n- **Further Tests:** Awaiting urine culture and sensitivity test results.\n- **Patient Education:** Discussed the importance of completing the antibiotic course and monitoring symptoms. Advised to seek immediate care if experiencing fever, severe abdominal pain, or other concerning symptoms. }}<|eot_id|>\n\n###Response B:\n{{ 1/2018\nHPC: UTI\nHPC: Nil\nHPC: UTI\nHPC: Nil\nHPC: UTI\nHPC: Nil\nHPC: UTI\nHPC: Nil\nHPC: UTI\nHPC: Nil\nHPC: UTI\nHPC: Nil\nHPC: UTI\nHPC: Nil\nHPC: UTI\nHPC: Nil\nHPC: UTI\nHPC: Nil\nHPC: UTI\nHPC: Nil\nHPC: UTI\nHPC: Nil\nHPC: UTI\nHP